                <pb facs="0448" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.44A15/164</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-04-09">April 9, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador called to see me this afternoon. The Ambassador said that
                    the British Foreign Office desired him to let me know that they were most
                    grateful for the suggestion I had made with regard to the Belize controversy
                    between Great Britain and Guatemala and that instructions had been sent to the
                    British Minister in Guatemala City to undertake conversations or negotiations
                    with the Guatemalan Foreign Minister to see whether some compromise or some way
                    out of the existing impasse with regard to the present British proposal might be
                    found.</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">elles</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
